{
  "rules": [
    "When sentiment is positive (≥0.2) in recent history, model tends to underpredict sharp upward moves — adjust forecast upward by 1–3% for the next 3–5 days.",
    "After a strong price spike (e.g., >85), model often overreacts and forecasts continued steep rise — cap forecast slope at 0.5–1.0% per day until sentiment stabilizes.",
    "If sentiment is consistently low (0.00) and price is trending down, model often fails to recognize mean reversion — add 0.5–1.5% upward bias for next 5–7 days.",
    "When model forecasts are flat or declining but true price rises sharply, sentiment history should trigger a 1–2% upward correction in next 3–5 days.",
    "For 30-day forecasts, if true outcome deviates >5% from model in first 5 days, apply a 1–2% upward adjustment for remaining horizon if sentiment remains neutral or positive.",
    "If sentiment history shows multiple 0.00 entries followed by a spike, model often misses the turn — forecast should be adjusted upward by 1–3% for next 3–7 days."
  ]
}
